'''''Trifolium cherleri''''', the '''cupped clover''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Fabaceae]].<ref name="1_of_913_Google_Scholar_results" >{{cite book |title=The Manual of Australian Agriculture |last1=Reid |first1=Robert L. |date=22 October 2013 |publisher= Butterworths |isbn=9781483100340 |page=270 }}</ref> It is native to the Canary Islands, the Mediterranean, and the Middle East as far east as Iran, and it has been introduced to Australia as a forage.<ref name="522998-1" >{{cite POWO |id=522998-1 |title=''Trifolium cherleri'' L. |access-date=28 April 2022 }}</ref> Three cultivars have been developed in Australia; 'Beenong', 'Yamina' and 'Lisare'.<ref name="1_of_913_Google_Scholar_results" />

